                <pb facs="0951" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg831"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root informs Mr. Meyer that many influential Hebrews in this country are
                    endeavoring to raise relief funds, being greatly distressed over the reports of
                    Jewish loss of life and suffering in the recent outbreaks. Requests him to
                    furnish as accurate report of these occurrences as possible, giving the number
                    of killed, wounded, sick, and destitute, and the losses sustained.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
